            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"(a) Except as provided in paragraph (b) of this section, the driver of a commercial motor vehicle specified in paragraphs (a) (1) through (6) of this section shall not cross a railroad track or tracks at grade unless he/she first: Stops the commercial motor vehicle within 50 feet of, and not closer than 15 feet to, the tracks\",\n        \"(b) A stop need not be made at:\",\n        \"(1) A streetcar crossing, or railroad tracks used exclusively for industrial switching purposes, within a business district, as defined in § 390.5 of this chapter.\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) introduces the stopping duty with 'Except as provided in paragraph (b) of this section', and paragraph (b)(1) specifies that a stop need not be made at streetcar crossings or industrial switching tracks in a business district. Setting relation to 'exception' and qualifying baseline claim C0000 correctly operationalizes this prose caveat into an explicit qualification relationship while preserving all existing fields.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"(a) Except as provided in paragraph (b) of this section, the driver of a commercial motor vehicle specified in paragraphs (a) (1) through (6) of this section shall not cross a railroad track or tracks at grade unless he/she first: Stops the commercial motor vehicle within 50 feet of, and not closer than 15 feet to, the tracks\",\n        \"(b) A stop need not be made at:\",\n        \"(2) A railroad grade crossing when a police officer or crossing flagman directs traffic to proceed.\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (b)(2) provides an explicit exception to the paragraph (a) stopping duty when a police officer or flagman directs traffic to proceed. Updating C0010 to have relation 'exception' qualifying baseline C0000 faithfully connects the exception to its targeted baseline duty.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"(a) Except as provided in paragraph (b) of this section, the driver of a commercial motor vehicle specified in paragraphs (a) (1) through (6) of this section shall not cross a railroad track or tracks at grade unless he/she first: Stops the commercial motor vehicle within 50 feet of, and not closer than 15 feet to, the tracks\",\n        \"(b) A stop need not be made at:\",\n        \"(3) A railroad grade crossing controlled by a functioning highway traffic signal transmitting a green indication which, under local law, permits the commercial motor vehicle to proceed across the railroad tracks without slowing or stopping.\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (b)(3) exempts vehicles from stopping when a functioning green highway traffic signal permits proceeding without stopping under local law. Linking this claim to C0000 with relation 'exception' accurately reflects the structural caveat in paragraph (a).\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"(a) Except as provided in paragraph (b) of this section, the driver of a commercial motor vehicle specified in paragraphs (a) (1) through (6) of this section shall not cross a railroad track or tracks at grade unless he/she first: Stops the commercial motor vehicle within 50 feet of, and not closer than 15 feet to, the tracks\",\n        \"(b) A stop need not be made at:\",\n        \"(4) An abandoned railroad grade crossing which is marked with a sign indicating that the rail line is abandoned.\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (b)(4) establishes that a stop need not be made at marked abandoned crossings, directly excepting drivers from the general grade-crossing stop rule in paragraph (a) (C0000). Setting relation to 'exception' qualifying C0000 is fully supported.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0004\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"(a) Except as provided in paragraph (b) of this section, the driver of a commercial motor vehicle specified in paragraphs (a) (1) through (6) of this section shall not cross a railroad track or tracks at grade unless he/she first: Stops the commercial motor vehicle within 50 feet of, and not closer than 15 feet to, the tracks\",\n        \"(b) A stop need not be made at:\",\n        \"(5) An industrial or spur line railroad grade crossing marked with a sign reading “Exempt.”\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (b)(5) exempts industrial or spur line crossings marked 'Exempt' from the grade-crossing stopping requirement stated in paragraph (a). Adding the edge linking C0013 as an exception qualifying C0000 is accurate and fully supported by the text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
